  "configuration_id": "config_007",
  "reason": "With no completed experiments, the primary uncertainty is whether multimodal fusion provides a meaningful advantage over single-modality baselines, and what a reasonable reference performance looks like. Config_007 (multimodal, singleprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, no aggregation, concat) is a clean, standard multimodal setup: it uses a well-established learned RNA encoder (scvi_n200), a standard image backbone (ResNet-50), the simplest profile setting, and the simplest fusion (concat) without additional aggregation. This isolates the core multimodal-fusion question while keeping other design dimensions at their simplest defaults, so any future performance change can be attributed to a specific modification. It establishes a reference point against which we can later compare single-modality baselines (to quantify the fusion gain) and more complex variants (multiprofile, transformer aggregation, weighted fusion, ViT-L image encoder) to determine which design axes actually matter under a limited budget."
}

